{"author":{"uri":{"label":"https://itunes.apple.com/ca/reviews/id41338197"}, "name":{"label":"🔥👉👌💯😩💯👌👈🔥"}, "label":""}, "updated":{"label":"2017-05-18T12:19:12-07:00"}, "im:rating":{"label":"5"}, "im:version":{"label":"3.0.1"}, "id":{"label":"1617425808"}, "title":{"label":"A Delight to Use!"}, "content":{"label":"I tried using Things several years ago but wasn't impressed by its then-too-simple organization of to-dos. I felt that I needed OmniFocus's more complex system to organize my tasks. Hoever, I never particularly enjoyed using OF since it always felt like a chore. I yearned for the simplicity of Things, but needed some more features.\n\nFinally, after years in development, Things 3 has come out. It's fantastic for so many reasons: the clean and intuitive UI; the easy-to-use Magic Plus feature; the addition of timely reminders; the Upcoming view; and desktop-like batch-editing feature on iOS. It's a joy to use and look at and doesn't bear any of the complexity that OF contains. The Watch app is also very minimalist with enough features to make it practically useful on your wrist.\n\nPurchasing the complete trio of apps (macOS, iPhone, and iPad) isn't cheap but for those who take their task management seriously, the price is well worth it to support a small-time developer. No subscription or hidden in-app trickery here.\n\nThe built-in Today/Upcoming/Scheduled views match my workflow perfectly. Cultured Code has outdone themselves here. It was a long time coming, but well worth it.", "attributes":{"type":"text"}}, "link":{"attributes":{"rel":"related", "href":"https://itunes.apple.com/ca/review?id=904237743&type=Purple%20Software"}}, "im:voteSum":{"label":"1"}, "im:contentType":{"attributes":{"term":"Application", "label":"Application"}}, "im:voteCount":{"label":"1"}}, 
